{
  "name": "Building materials",
  "icon": "slimic:slimic_stone_bricks",
  "category": "slimic:world",
  "sortnum": 2,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "The Slimic Blocks tab contains 32 base materials plus 8 stairs, 8 slabs, and 6 walls. Gather natural stone, slate, soil, silt, clay, mud, and gel in The Slimic. Use the matching pickaxe or shovel; Slimic Stone drops Slimic Cobblestone without Silk Touch."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "A stonecutter turns Slimic Stone into decorative masonry. Matching stair, slab, and wall recipes also work in a crafting table. Smelt Slimic Cobblestone back into stone, fire silt into Gel Glass, or dry congealed slime in a furnace."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Mix native planks with a slimeball for Slime-Infused Planks. Clay and a slimeball make Slimic Clay; congealed slime and a clay ball make Hardened Slime. A hoe tills Slimic Soil, Damp Grass, or Slime Mud with clear space above into ordinary farmland."
    }
  ],
